<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariano Arista</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1802">1802</a>–<a href="/years/1855">1855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariano Arista was a Mexican general and politician who was President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1851 to 1853. In 1840 he defeated the federalist rebels of the Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>. Commanding the Army of the North at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican–American War</a>, he lost the battles of Palo Alto and Resaca de la <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a> in May 1846.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariano-arista.jpg" alt="Mariano Arista" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Édouard Pingret · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariano_Arista,_Presidente_de_la_Rep%C3%BAblica_de_1851_a_1853.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
